# EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR: A quote inside '{$...}' ends the string early
#~
A quote inside an interpolation ends the string literal there: the scanner
stops a string at its first unescaped '"', so "x: {$(Join(items, ", "))}" is
the string 'x: {$(Join(items, ' followed by tokens no statement can start
with. The parser's statement list called ParseStatement on that same token
again and again without consuming it, allocating nodes each time, so obc ran
until it was killed (near 16 GB) instead of reporting anything.

Now a statement that consumes nothing makes the list step past its token, and
a string left inside an open '{$' is reported as what it is, with the fix:
compute the value into a local first. The regression runner's compile has a
time limit, so a return of the hang fails this test rather than stalling it.
~#

class QuoteInInterpolation {
  function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
    items := ["a", "b"];
    "x: {$(String->Join(items, ", "))}"->PrintLine();
  }
}
